        "abstract": "In this paper, the trend and variability of minimal size 65nm NMOS and PMOS transistors are measured and analyzed from 292K to 9.5K (for PMOS) and 4.2K (for NMOS). The changes and variability of the on-state current, threshold voltage, linear resistance, output resistance, and transconductance, which are important for analog applications, are extracted and analyzed. Empirical quadratic equations are developed to model the trend which can be used as handy tools for estimation. A simple methodology for rapidly calibrating the 4.2K BSIM model for the on-state currents of 65nm transistors is also proposed and demonstrated.",
